-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 68: define the `related_note` edge table as a proper
--   TYPE RELATION FROM note TO note
-- so the auto-link feature (Track Y) can persist note↔note similarity links as
-- real graph edges that can be RELATEd, traversed, drawn and exported.
--
-- Background. Track Y (auto-link) finds a note's most-similar other notes by
-- embedding cosine and stores each link as a `related_note` edge. The table is
-- BRAND NEW — no prior migration defines it — so on any DB (fresh container or
-- staging) it would otherwise be auto-created by the first RELATE as the
-- SurrealDB default
--   DEFINE TABLE related_note TYPE ANY SCHEMALESS
-- which stores an untyped record, NOT a graph edge. This is the exact class the
-- `mentions`/`cites` drift migrations (66/67) fixed; 68 defines it correctly up
-- front so the auto-link writer always lands a typed `note -> related_note ->
-- note` edge.
--
-- Strategy (mirrors migrations 66/67's non-destructive remediation):
--   1. DELETE only null-endpoint junk rows (in = NONE OR out = NONE). A real
--      `related_note` edge always has non-null in/out, so this is a no-op on a
--      healthy table and only clears the non-edge junk a drifted/auto-created
--      TYPE ANY table could hold (which would otherwise block the RELATION
--      redefine). A blanket `DELETE related_note` would WIPE healthy edges — the
--      destructive mistake migration 58 made; 62/66/67 fixed it with this
--      null-endpoint-only predicate and 68 follows suit.
--   2. DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE ... TYPE RELATION FROM note TO note. On SurrealDB
--      v2 OVERWRITE converts a drifted/auto-created TYPE ANY table to RELATION;
--      on an already-correct RELATION table it re-asserts the identical
--      definition and PRESERVES existing edge records (the migration-62/66/67
--      empirical fact, re-checked for `related_note` by this track's container
--      tests). `related_note` is a regenerated projection (auto-link clears and
--      re-relates per note), so there is no canonical edge state worth a
--      destructive rollback.
--   3. DEFINE the edge fields with OVERWRITE. `similarity_score` is the cosine
--      that drove the link (the per-edge "why", for thresholding the viz / triage,
--      parallel to `mentions.weight` / `cites.confidence`). `method` records how
--      the link was derived (`"embedding"` today; a future path could add
--      another). `created_at` mirrors migrations 66/67 for provenance parity.
--
-- Strict-field / S.4 note. Every strict field below carries a DEFAULT, and the
-- table is EMPTY on every existing DB (it is brand new — 0 rows everywhere), so
-- there are NO pre-existing rows to drift and NO backfill UPDATE is required
-- (the S.4 hazard is a strict field with no default added to a table that
-- already holds rows; neither condition applies here). The auto-link writer
-- supplies `similarity_score`/`method` explicitly via RELATE-with-SET, so the
-- DEFAULTs are a safety floor, never the live value.
--
-- Idempotent + forward-only: the DELETE matches nothing on a second pass and
-- every OVERWRITE re-asserts an identical definition. Down is a documented
-- no-op (a schema definition has no faithful inverse; reverting to TYPE ANY
-- would re-break `RELATE note -> related_note -> note` — the very correctness
-- this establishes — and the edge set is a regenerated projection).
-- ============================================================================

-- 1. Drop ONLY null-endpoint junk rows (the non-edge records a drifted/
--    auto-created TYPE ANY table could hold). Real `related_note` edges always
--    have non-null in/out, so this never touches them — no-op on a fresh empty
--    table AND on any healthy edge set.
DELETE related_note WHERE in = NONE OR out = NONE;

-- 2. Assert the canonical edge definition. Converts a drifted/auto-created
--    TYPE ANY table to RELATION note->note on v2; identical no-op (edges
--    preserved) on an already-correct RELATION table.
DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE related_note SCHEMAFULL TYPE RELATION FROM note TO note;

-- 3. Edge fields (all strict WITH defaults — S.4 safe). `similarity_score` is the
--    cosine similarity that drove the link; `method` is how it was derived
--    (`"embedding"` today); `created_at` is provenance (mirrors 66/67).
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE similarity_score ON related_note TYPE float DEFAULT 0.0;
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE method ON related_note TYPE string DEFAULT "embedding";
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE created_at ON related_note TYPE datetime DEFAULT time::now();

-- Index on similarity_score so the auto-link triage / viz can threshold edges
-- (mirrors idx_mentions_weight / idx_cites_confidence). OVERWRITE so a re-apply
-- converges.
DEFINE INDEX OVERWRITE idx_related_note_score ON related_note FIELDS similarity_score;
